    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "On basis of statements, it would not be evident that neither there was an alarm nor intention to provoke the applicant and so far as offence under Section 498-A is concerned only reference is that applicant No.1 has harassed her physically and mentally without any specific averment, therefore, in view of judgment passed by Supreme Court in case of Lalankumar Singh and others vs. State of Maharashtra, 2022 SCC Online SCC 1383, a case is made out for interference and accordingly, impugned order is set aside, however, considering that this order is passed without issuing notice to opposite party No.2 i.e. complainant, therefore matter is remitted back to learned Magistrate to pass fresh order after taking note of judgment passed by Supreme Court in Lalankumar Singh and others (supra) as well as above referred observations.\n5. Accordingly, application is disposed of with aforesaid observation.\nOrder Date :- 15.7.2024 P. Pandey  Abhigyan @ Abhijnan Basu vs State Of U.P. And Another on 15 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/192950790/\n3",
